> zefciu wrote:
> > - Melee is rarely optimal
> > 	use ranged weapons and polearms

> If you are a melee character, then Ranged is rarely necessary.

Agreed, up to a point.

For any individual battle, ranged attack is almost always
preferable, since it means no loss of hit points on your part.
If the monster has some special attack, or your hit points are
low, ranged attacks are the only acceptable solution.  The
problem, however, is that all ranged attacks use up important
resources (generally temporarily), where as melee doesn't.  So
if I can melee well, I'll generally favor it in the general
case, to be sure that I still have the resources if a case
occurs where I definitly must use a ranged attack immediately
after the battle.

And of course, there will be special cases.  At present, I've a
knight dual weaponing +6 Excalibur and a katana.  Melee is
generally the preferred option, but when I hit the castle, and
played the tune to open the drawbridge (with the idea of raising
it each time a real nasty came out), the first monster out was a
stone giant.  I killed him with melee, and then safely wiped out
all of the others (including a Lich or two) with magic missles
from behind the stone, simply waiting for regeneration each time
my mana got low.  (It was especially nice as I had two succobi
on the level above, so I could increase my XP while I waited.)

